, Helsinki"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/59041"} "20 from 14 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Between 1949-51, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78426"} "Jim Fuchs"] ", bronze medalist at the " [:a {:href "/results/58668"} "1948 Olympics"] ", was the world’s best shot putter, winning 88 consecutive meets, and breaking the world record four times. However, at the 1951 AAUs, he was beaten by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78854"} "Parry O’Brien"] ". O’Brien in turn was beaten at the 1952 US Trials by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78567"} "Darrow Hooper"] ". But at the Trials, only two inches separated Fuchs, O’Brien, and Hooper, so an American sweep was considered likely."] "\n\n" [:p {} "O’Brien opened the final with 17.41 (57-1½), and this would be good enough for the gold medal. In the final round, Hooper put a scare into him, with 17.39 (57-0¾), but had to settle for silver. Fuchs second consecutive bronze medal gave the US another sweep in the shot put – its sixth one."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1035"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78854"} "Parry O'Brien"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "16.05 (1)"] [:td {} "17.41 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1034"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78567"} "Darrow Hooper"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA